    "code_snippet": "func compareForkENR(self, peer *enr.Record) error {\n  if !bytes.Equal(peerEntry.CurrentForkDigest, selfEntry.CurrentForkDigest) { return errCurrentDigestMismatch }\n  if peerEntry.NextForkEpoch != selfEntry.NextForkEpoch {\n    // Log trace, return nil -- peer accepted despite incompatible fork view!\n    return nil\n  }\n  if !bytes.Equal(peerEntry.NextForkVersion, selfEntry.NextForkVersion) { return errNextVersionMismatch }\n  if !params.FuluEnabled() { return nil }\n  // FuluEnabled() check for nfd: TOCTOU window at fork activation\n  if peerNFD != selfNFD { return errNextDigestMismatch }\n}",
    "state_context": "compareForkENR returns nil (connection allowed) when NextForkEpoch mismatches. This allows peers that have set FarFutureEpoch (no-fork sentinel) to connect regardless of local fork schedule. FuluEnabled() is evaluated at call time with no atomicity guarantee across concurrent evaluations.",
